From e5543fe9de1caf63193fa850c80a9063e07b9c31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/41] Tab5: "TX locked: Another Device has the transmitter"

The relay now tells the Tab5 when another device has the transmitter, so the
Tab5 can say so instead of "transmitting" bursts the relay drops. A new
QMXR/1 frame TX_LOCK (type 12: u8 locked [+ reason text]) goes to the Tab5
right after the HELLO (which now says txlock=1), when the Mac's TCI bridge
connects or leaves, and on the 1 s ping tick (so the tab5-tx-always flag file
takes effect without a reconnect).

While locked the Tab5:
* FT8/FT4: refuses to arm, and does not key a burst armed before the lock;
  a relay refusal (TX_DONE status 2) caught in between says the same;
* WSPR: refuses at arm and at the burst;
* Tune (screen and web) and power calibration: refuse;
* shows "TX locked: Another Device has the transmitter" in amber on the FT8
  screen's TX label, in the FT8 status line, as a toast, and on the web page
  (state tx_locked).
An older relay never sends TX_LOCK, and over USB it is always unlocked.

The relay also counts Tune (MD8;) as keying: it is dropped from the Tab5 while
locked, and while the Tab5 is tuning, port 3 (the Mac) cannot key.

Bench test with the fake radio: TX_LOCK 0 after the HELLO, 1 when a TCI
listener (tx=1) connected, 0 when it left; MD8;, TX;, TA1500.00; and a burst
from the Tab5 were BLOCKED while locked (burst: TX_DONE 2); a port-3 TX; was
BLOCKED while the Tab5 was in MD8 and passed after MD6. Firmware files
compile-checked against the ESP-IDF toolchain.

